LC 128 — Longest Consecutive Sequence
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Put all numbers in a set.
Start counting only when x - 1 is not present.
Count consecutive numbers.

Algorithm:
Put all numbers in set

For each number:
    if x-1 doesn't exist:
        count consecutive numbers
        update maximum


CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    int longestConsecutive(vector<int>& nums) {
        unordered_set<int> s(nums.begin(), nums.end());
        int ans = 0;

        for (int x : s) {
            if (!s.count(x - 1)) {
                int y = x, len = 1;

                while (s.count(y + 1))
                    y++, len++;

                ans = max(ans, len);
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

EX:
nums = [100,4,200,1,3,2]

Set = {100,4,200,1,3,2}

1 → no 0 → start
1 → 2 → 3 → 4

Length = 4

Answer = 4 ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n) average
Space: O(n)
